course: dictionary
lesson: 5250
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Jogging can mean running slowly for exercise, or it can mean giving something a little push. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Professional midfielders often cover about 10 to 12 km in a match, in a mix of walking, jogging and sprinting.» Walking is slow and sprinting is very fast, so jogging must be somewhere in between: running slowly and steadily.
explain: Ask yourself: does this fit the sentence? Try the meaning you think is right and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one. Here, «running slowly and steadily» fits, but «pushing gently» does not.
explain: Phrases can change the meaning too. «Jog someone's memory» means help them remember something. Nobody is running there and nobody is pushing anything. The whole phrase has its own meaning, so read the phrase as one unit.
fact: Jogging, as a noun, means running slowly and steadily for exercise.
fact: As a verb, jog (jogs, jogged, jogging) can mean to push or knock something gently, as in «Don't jog my arm».
fact: «Jog someone's memory» means help them remember something.
fact: Jogging is good for your heart, which is why PE teachers and doctors often recommend it.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, check the words around it before you decide.
exercise: «Professional midfielders often cover about 10 to 12 km in a match, in a mix of walking, jogging and sprinting.» What does jogging mean in this sentence? | *Running slowly and steadily | Kicking the ball hard | Standing still and resting | Running as fast as possible
exercise: Sam says «Don't jog my arm» means run round the park. What does jog mean here? | *To push or knock something gently | To shout loudly | To run round the park | To lift something up high
exercise: Which phrase means help someone remember something? | jogging with friends | a jogging track | go jogging | *jog someone's memory
test: «Every morning Mia goes jogging before school to keep her heart healthy.» What does jogging mean here? | Walking very slowly to school | Sitting quietly in the park | *Running slowly and steadily for exercise | Pushing someone gently
test: «Could you jog my memory about the date of the trip?» What does jog mean here? | *To help someone remember | To knock something over | To run around the field | To shout the date loudly
exam: Which sentence uses jogging as a noun, meaning running for exercise? | Please don't jogging my arm while I write | The jogging of the stone made the water ripple | *Dad likes jogging in the park before breakfast | Jog the pencil gently across the page
